@Foreman12346  Drop the insult, and the owner will pick it up. Did I even say once that China was collapsing or anything like that?

The U.S. market crashing in the 2008 financial crisis was not a collapse moment, but it was not good news for the country as well. It's the same thing in China. When the hell did I say that China will collapse?

China has other problems, like its demographic collapse or its property sector collapse, which are much more reflective of the situation of the country in that sense. The stock market collapse is just one among many.
